' 19 PathMap keys: the path, the path key and the prefix keys of one channel.
'
' Source of Figure N11.7a in ../design.md (section N11.7). The figure restates
' channel_path, encode_path and EncodedPath of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/pathmap/path_codec.rs (P5e). It adds no
' new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The channel @[0, 1, 2] is a plain list, so its path holds its elements.
'   2. One buffer holds the path key and the end of each prefix key.
'   3. The datum lives on D(sid, path_key), and the markers and the waiters
'      of each prefix live on I(sid, prefix_key) (wave W3).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 19-pathmap-keys.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 19-pathmap-keys
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ObjectBorderColor $rrs_relation
title The keys of the path [0, 1, 2]

object "channel @[0, 1, 2]" as channel $rrs_name
object "path p = [0, 1, 2]" as path $rrs_object
object "path_key(p)\n03 00 · 03 02 · 03 04 · 00" as key $rrs_storage
object "prefix keys of p\nε · 03 00 · 03 00 03 02 · 03 00 03 02 03 04" as prefixes $rrs_storage
object "D(sid, path_key(p))\nthe datum" as data $rrs_substrate
object "I(sid, prefix_key(q)) for each q ⪯ p\nthe markers and the waiters (W3)" as index $rrs_substrate

channel --> path : channel_path
path --> key : encode_path
path --> prefixes : EncodedPath::prefix_keys
key --> data : the data channel
prefixes --> index : the index channels
@enduml
